# Two records of one kind match when their current versions share an NDC, or the same chosen RxNorm code. A version's
# chosen RxNorm code is its rec:selectedCode when that is an RxNorm code, else its only RxNorm code; one with several
# RxNorm codes and none selected chooses none, and an NDC it selected does not stop its only RxNorm code being the
# chosen one. NDC is a separate way to match: a shared NDC is enough, whichever code a version selected. No table is
# read. A shared RxNorm code is not checked to be a product, so two records coded only with one ingredient's code
# match, as they did when this rule compared RxNorm codes alone; that is carried from version 5 until
# jayostis/cascade-vocabulary#121, when this rule joins on a shared RxNorm code only when the held tables show it is
# a product (SCD, SBD, GPCK, BPCK), and any other shared code becomes a review item for a person to confirm. An NDC
# names a package within one listing; NDC product codes have been reassigned after a product was discontinued, and
# dates are ignored here, so a pod spanning years may join two products under one reused NDC, a known limit. Any
# intents are ignored. Each ordered pair is a row. Every pair this rule joins shares a code, and the rule that reads
# the brand generics table joins only records that share none, so no pair is judged by both.
PREFIX clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#>
PREFIX pav: <http://purl.org/pav/>
PREFIX rec: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/records/v1-draft#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?record ?other
WHERE {
  ?record rec:kind ?kind ; pav:hasCurrentVersion ?version .
  ?other rec:kind ?kind ; pav:hasCurrentVersion ?otherVersion .
  ?version rec:ndcCode|rec:selectedCode|clinical:rxNormCode ?code .
  ?otherVersion rec:ndcCode|rec:selectedCode|clinical:rxNormCode ?code .
  FILTER (?record != ?other)
  FILTER (EXISTS { ?version rec:ndcCode ?code . ?otherVersion rec:ndcCode ?code }
          || ((EXISTS { ?version rec:selectedCode ?code }
               || (NOT EXISTS { ?version rec:selectedCode ?selected
                                FILTER (STRSTARTS(STR(?selected), "http://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/rxnorm/")) }
                   && NOT EXISTS { ?version clinical:rxNormCode ?another FILTER (?another != ?code) }))
              && (EXISTS { ?otherVersion rec:selectedCode ?code }
                  || (NOT EXISTS { ?otherVersion rec:selectedCode ?selected
                                   FILTER (STRSTARTS(STR(?selected), "http://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/umls/rxnorm/")) }
                      && NOT EXISTS { ?otherVersion clinical:rxNormCode ?another FILTER (?another != ?code) }))))
}
